    "brick.wait": {
      "comment": "One block (brick) in the list of a design's program, read as an instruction. Shown on screen and spoken by VoiceOver. Pauses the program. %@ is a value that may be a number, a variable name or a small formula such as \"360 ÷ Inner Loop\", already formatted. This form is used when the value is a formula, a variable or a fraction. Word order is yours: the value is interpolated, not appended.",
